Installation: 
============== 
To install, adjust the variables in the script file <Install_density>. The script 
is based on bash shell. For different shell. The script sets the necesary variable and makes the
density program as a new application of the atsp2k pachage.

requirements:
-------------
density needs atsp2k libraries and lapack

preparation:
------------

#extract the files from the .tar in a temporary directory
mkdir density
cd density
tar -cvf density.tar
#this creates (among others) the subdirectory /src, which contains the source files of density.

#go to the atsp2k main directore and set the ATSP environment variable:
cd /my_atsp2k/
export ATSP=$( pwd )

#the src files (supplied in /src directory of tar file) should be copied to the
#correct location in the atsp2K directory structure:
#a) make a new directory
mkdir ${ATSP}/src/appl/density

#b) copy the source files and the Makefile from the /src directory created by expanding the .tar file) e.g.
# replace ${TEMPDIR} with the relevant directory e.g. /density/src 
cp /density/src/* ${ATSP}/src/appl/density  

#copy the Install_density script from /density/ to /my_atsp2k/
cp /density/Install_density ${ATSP}

#once the files in place the environment variables can be exported:
export FC="pgf90"                          # Fortran compiler
export FC_FLAGS="-mcmodel=medium -Msave -O3 -fastsse"
                                           # compiler flags
export FC_LD="-Bstatic"                    # Serial linker flags

# the density program uses a lapack routine, so the compiler needs an extra flag
export LAPACK_LIB="-lpthread -lacml"

# setting the variables in ${ATSP}/src/density/Makefile
EXED = ${ATSP}/bin           #sets the default binary directory of atsp2k
LIBDIR = ${ATSP}/lib         #sets the default library directory of atsp2k
EXEF = $(EXED)/density       #sets the binary to be built
RCA = -lang -lcom            #sets flags for reference to atsp2k libraries
 
building:
---------
#enter density directory
cd ${ATSP}/src/appl/density

# make the density program
make $* 2>&1 | tee ${ATSP}/make.err
grep "severe" ./make.err

# return to atsp main directory
cd ${ATSP}

Testing:
=========
The directory Test has contains input and output files for a Be atom n=3 CAS-MCHF calculation.
Note: take care with machine dependency of non formatted data files.
